{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Arise, go up to Beit El.</b> Rashi explained: because you delayed on the way you were punished, and this came upon you through your daughter. And if you ask: earlier, regarding 'his eleven children,' Rashi himself explained that because he withheld her from his brother Esav — perhaps she would restore him to the better path — therefore he was punished through her, since in the end she fell into the hand of Shekhem. One may answer: this depends on that: as soon as he returned from Paddan Aram he should have given her to Esav, perhaps he would repent through her. And because he went and withheld her from Esav and kept avoiding Shekhem, on the way to Sukkot and Beit El, he was delaying his vow."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {0 "The abbreviations פירש״י, וא״ת, and שע״י are resolved as 'Rashi explained,' 'and if you ask,' and 'because of / through,' respectively."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:07:22.375785666Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}